		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=36038#p36038"><![CDATA[
I myself haven't implemented EPA, but if it's possible to identify the features that produce a point of contact then the caching of data from one point to another can happen through some book-keeping, like a check for matching contact point IDs. This would avoid any annoying threshold tweaking.<br><br>As for the manifold not being very stable the first few frames due to the manifold having only one or two points (edit: well in 2D just one point would be unstable a lot of the time, but in 3D sometimes 4 or 5 points is necessary)... This is just a limitation of the GJK/EPA algorithms.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=10235">RandyGaul</a> — Thu Aug 06, 2015 3:18 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
